# 16. Security requirements

Apply appropriate security practices.

- Validate requests on the server
- Enforce authorization on the server
- Configure Firestore security rules
- Restrict administrative write operations
- Verify Firebase identity tokens
- Use trusted server-side authorization for admin roles
- Validate attachment types and sizes
- Sanitize unsafe user content
- Protect contact and quote submission endpoints against spam
- Use rate limiting
- Protect secrets with environment configuration
- Avoid sensitive customer information in logs
- Do not trust client-provided order totals
- Prevent unauthorized access to customer quotes and orders

Include basic security-focused tests for authorization and validation behavior.

