# 17. SEO and accessibility

Implement good SEO foundations:
- Semantic HTML
- Descriptive page titles
- Page-level metadata
- Canonical URLs
- Open Graph metadata
- Descriptive image alt text
- Sitemap
- robots.txt
- Structured data where genuinely applicable
- Clean route names
- Logical heading hierarchy

Keep in mind that a purely client-rendered React application can have SEO limitations.

Structure metadata and routes so the project can adopt prerendering or server rendering in a future production phase if necessary.

Accessibility:
- Proper labels
- Visible keyboard focus
- Keyboard-accessible navigation
- Accessible dropdowns and dialogs
- Sufficient color contrast
- WCAG 2.2 AA as the target
- Reduced-motion support
- Meaningful form validation errors
- Logical tab order
- Screen-reader-friendly status messages

